│ patch_name               │ collective_phase_mixers                                                                   │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the overparameterized, qubit-specific block with a permutation-consistent         │
│                          │ collective mixer. Each rotation angle is shared across all eight qubits, reducing the     │
│                          │ circuit from 146 to 20 total trainable parameters while retaining independent parameters  │
│                          │ for each repeated block. The fixed all-pairs IsingZZ feature map already supplies         │
│                          │ data-dependent entanglement, so the additional line of CZ gates is unnecessary and        │
│                          │ imposes an artificial ordering on the qubits. The RY layer creates interference paths,    │
│                          │ the RZ layer controls their relative phases, and the terminal RX converts phase           │
│                          │ information into the measured Z populations. Unlike the seed's terminal RZ layer, the     │
│                          │ final RX remains directly observable by the readout. This should improve parameter        │
│                          │ efficiency, reduce overfitting and circuit depth, and accelerate Adam convergence while   │
│                          │ preserving the symmetry naturally matched by the mean-Z readout.                          │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
