│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ commutation_tied_rz                                                                       │
│ patch_description        │ Tie each post-entangler RZ angle to the corresponding pre-entangler angle. Every RZ       │
│                          │ commutes with the CZ line, so the original block depends only on the sum of each wire's   │
│                          │ pre/post angles; keeping them independent wastes one parameter per qubit without adding   │
│                          │ expressivity. Reusing the parameter keys preserves the same reachable effective rotations │
│                          │ while reducing parameters per block from 24 to 16 and total parameters from 146 to 98.    │
│                          │ Applying the shared angle twice also retains the favorable effective update scale of the  │
│                          │ redundant parametrization, helping preserve convergence speed while improving parameter   │
│                          │ efficiency and reducing overfitting risk.                                                 │
