│ patch_name               │ lean_brickwall_ring_ansatz                                                                │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the 3-rotation-layer + chain-CZ design with a 2-rotation-layer (RY+RZ) +          │
│                          │ brick-wall ring CZ design. This removes the redundant post-CZ RZ layer (redundancy arises │
│                          │ because with N_REPEATS=2, the next block's RY+RZ already provides full rotation after     │
│                          │ CZ). The brick-wall CZ creates a ring topology in just 2 parallel layers instead of 7     │
│                          │ sequential steps, significantly reducing depth. Parameters drop from 24→16 per block      │
│                          │ (146→98 total), gates from 31→24 per block, and depth per block from ~10→4. The design    │
│                          │ maintains full expressibility through the Euler-angle-complete RY+RZ rotation and ring    │
│                          │ entanglement topology.                                                                    │
