│ patch_name               │ shared_bridge_crx                                                                         │
│ patch_description        │ This design retains the strong RY–RZ–CZ–RZ structure while making a low-parameter,        │
│                          │ strictly more expressive extension. The commuting CZ chain is scheduled as two disjoint   │
│                          │ matchings, reducing circuit depth without changing its unitary when the new controlled    │
│                          │ rotations are zero.                                                                       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Each alternating bridge CZ is immediately followed by a CRX. All three CRX gates share    │
│                          │ one parameter per block, so the total rises only from 16 to 17 parameters per block (104  │
│                          │ parameters including readout). CRX does not commute with the phase feature map or the     │
│                          │ surrounding Z rotations, allowing graph-dependent phases to be converted into measurable  │
│                          │ populations earlier. Sharing the bridge parameter regularizes this added capacity and     │
│                          │ aggregates its gradient across the chain.                                                 │
