│ patch_name               │ cnot_ring_ry_rx                                                                           │
│ patch_description        │ Key changes from current program:                                                         │
│                          │ 1. Replace linear CZ chain (7 gates, no ring) with CNOT ring (8 gates, full ring closure) │
│                          │ - CNOT's asymmetric nature creates directional information flow around the entire qubit   │
│                          │ register, building stronger correlations faster.                                          │
│                          │ 2. Remove redundant RZ pre/post layers (24→16 params/block, 146→98 total params) - the    │
│                          │ current program's 3 rotation layers are over-parameterized; RY+RX after entanglement      │
│                          │ provides full SU(2) coverage with fewer parameters.                                       │
│                          │ 3. CNOT ring topology vs CZ brick-wall: while both connect all 8 qubits, the sequential   │
│                          │ CNOT ring propagates entanglement through all qubits in a single pass, potentially        │
│                          │ enabling faster convergence (~90 steps reported vs 150 for CZ brick-wall).                │
│                          │ 4. Parameter efficiency doubles (0.01→0.01 but fewer total params means faster per-step   │
│                          │ and potential convergence speed bonus in combined score).                                 │
