│ patch_description        │ Redesigned ansatz using a brick-layer entanglement pattern with ring CNOT connectivity.   │
│                          │ The block alternates between even-pair CNOTs (0→1, 2→3, 4→5, 6→7) and odd-pair CNOTs      │
│                          │ (1→2, 3→4, 5→6, 7→0), sandwiching RY and RZ rotation layers between them. This creates a  │
│                          │ highly expressive circuit with efficient parameter usage (24 params per block) and strong │
│                          │ entanglement coverage across all qubits via the ring topology. The brick-layer pattern    │
│                          │ avoids barren plateaus better than fully random entanglement while ensuring information   │
│                          │ flows between all qubit pairs within two entangling layers.                               │
